<statement>
<p>
	Given the size of the square grid, N, this program displays the starting game board and returns the rectangle objects that represent each space on the grid.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>N</pf> (1 x 1) number — size of the N x N square grid.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>rects</pf> (N x N) number — array of rectangle objects.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>See the template and</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>class demos</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>for guidance on how to display the interface.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		Rect_objs = MS_display_interface_Key(6)
		Rect_objs =
		6×6 Rectangle array:
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle    Rectangle
		and displays the following figure:
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
